      "releaseNotes": "New Avionics Tour for the A320 — explore the avionics compartment with interactive photo navigation and LRU descriptions\nDamage reports: cleaner interface and new Save & Close button\nMinor improvements across the app",
      "version": "1.0.3",
      "wrapperType": "software",
      "currency": "EUR",
      "description": "Aviation Maintenance Tools is a professional maintenance reference app for aircraft technicians, focused on A320 troubleshooting and ECAM reset procedures.\nIt provides fast, structured access to key information used during fault troubleshooting, reset procedures, structural damage report creation, and everyday maintenance tasks—helping technicians work more efficiently on the line or in base maintenance.\n\nECAM Fault Messages\n\n• Extensive database of fault messages with the associated circuit breakers (CBs) required for each A320 ECAM reset\n• Images of aircraft panels showing where to find each circuit breaker\n• Clear, step-by-step ECAM reset procedures with an integrated countdown\n• Maintenance manual and MEL references linked to each message\n\nQuick Fault Search\n\n• Instantly find messages using a fast search engine, reducing time-consuming searches during line maintenance calls\n• Browse messages organized by ATA chapter\n• Recent tab for quick access to previously viewed content\n\nAvionics Tour\n\n• Interactive photo tour of the A320neo avionics compartment\n• Navigate through AFT, FWD, LH MID and RH MID bays with real aircraft photos\n• Tap any LRU marker to view its name, location and technical description\n• Built-in search to quickly find any unit across the compartment\n\nStructural Damage Reports\n\n• Interactive structural damage report forms generator with support for multiple damage entries, eliminating paper notes and improving handover\n• Useful for reporting a single damage or multiple damages (e.g., after lightning events)\n• Attach damage photos taken with the device camera\n• Export reports to PDF or ZIP files (including images) to continue working on a computer or another phone with the app\n\nAlpha Callups\n\n• Complete list of Alpha Callups, filtered by engine model\n• Built-in search engine for quick searches\n\nElectrical Contacts\n\n• Electrical contacts, terminals, and splices part numbers library, with quick search function\n• Direct reference to the ESPM figure where each item is located\n• Crimping and insertion/extraction references included\n\nCommon Part Numbers\n\n• Commonly used aircraft part numbers organized by category and aircraft zone\n• Each part number can include a description and photos\n• Add your own part numbers with photos taken using the device camera\n• Create and share your custom part-number list with colleagues\n• Useful for quickly finding references during line maintenance\n\nMaintenance Manual References\n\n• Structured breakdown of the maintenance manual index\n• Fast search for quick lookup\n\nDisclaimer – Training & Reference Use Only\n\nThis app is designed for training, reference, and informational purposes only.\nThis app does not replace official documentation. Fault messages, reset procedures, structural damage reports, manual/MEL/ESPM references, electrical contact data, and part number information are provided as a learning aid for maintenance technicians.\nUsers must always consult the latest official manuals and procedures before performing any maintenance or operational task on an aircraft.\nThis app must not be used as the sole source for maintenance decisions.\n\nThis app is not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or an official product of any aircraft manufacturer.\nThe app does not copy, reproduce, or distribute proprietary manufacturer materials (including manual pages or documentation) and does not use manufacturer logos or branding.",
